/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Floorplanning fixes the physical frame before any cell moves.
   - Utilization measures how much core area is occupied.
   - U is utilization; Aused is area of blocks plus standard cells (fixed-height gate layouts); Acore is core area in mm²; W and H are core width and height in mm.
   - Placement assigns coordinates to every standard cell inside the core rows.
   - Clock-tree synthesis (CTS) runs after placement.
   - Routing turns connections into metal wires.
   - Crosstalk is unwanted coupling between nearby wires: an aggressor switches and injects a glitch or delay into a victim.
*/
