/* book exam traps: High utilization is not automatically good: above a point it causes routing congestion, detours and timing loss. | Placement is not routing: short placement wirelength can still route badly, and legal placement does not prove timing. | Global routing is not detailed routing: global assigns regions and estimates congestion; detailed picks exact tracks and vias. | DRC clean is not signoff clean: DRC checks geometry only; LVS, timing, power and IR drop are separate checks. | Clock skew is not always driven to zero: useful skew can improve timing, and insertion delay matters too. */
