/* book exam traps: A soft core is not software. It is synthesizable hardware RTL and still consumes LUTs, memories, DSP slices and power. | Hard IP is fixed to one fabrication process. You cannot copy GDSII to another foundry node without redesign. | Soft IP portability does not remove integration work: bus adaptation, clock-domain crossing, reset and timing closure remain. | Counting cores by lookup tables alone is wrong. Check every resource: DSP slices, block RAM, I/O pins and power. | A license is not ownership. Check modification, reuse and redistribution rights before shipping. */
